    "long_instructions": "##Explore and Explain\r\n\r\n1. In the **preview**, try out the color search:\r\n   - Type `blue`, `Blue`, ` blu`, and then clear the box so it’s empty.\r\n   - Observe what changes on the page (cards and match count).\r\n2. Open `script.js` and find the `searchColors(data, query)` function.\r\n3. Use the AI helper:\r\n   - Copy just the `searchColors` function into the chat.\r\n   - Ask at least **two focused questions**, such as:\r\n   \t- Where does the `query` value come from in this app?\r\n   \t- Why does this function convert both the query and the color name to lowercase?\r\n   \t- Why does this function build a `results` array instead of changing the original `data`?\r\n   \t- What happens when the query is an empty string (`\"\"`)? Why?\r\n4. After you get answers from AI, write short notes in comments **above `searchColors`** summarizing:\r\n   - How the function handles case differences.\r\n   - What it does for an empty query.\r\n   - Why it returns a new array instead of editing `colors`.",
    "name_suffix": "_2025-pilot"
  },
